# Ownership boundary — the trust-critical core.
#
# Build/patch agents MUST NOT be able to alter the deterministic checks,
# the exploit playbook, the claim/evidence schemas, or the gate wiring.
# These paths require review from the human owner. Combined with a protected
# `main` branch, this is the technical backbone of the "can't lie" trust model.
#
# Replace @owner with the real GitLab username before going public.

/verifier/      @owner
/redteam/       @owner
/schemas/       @owner
/flows/         @owner
/.gitlab-ci.yml @owner
/CODEOWNERS     @owner
